# SRG-APP-000131-WSR-000073  -  CAT II
# Expansion modules must be fully reviewed, tested, and signed before they
# can exist on a production web server.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000131-WSR-000073
group:           V-206373
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           D
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-003992
control_rev5:    CM-14

contribution:    Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 exposes no configuration setting that requires a
                 digital signature, a review record, or a test record on an app or
                 expansion module before it is loaded, so the application cannot decide
                 this requirement; the nearest controls it does hold - confining who may
                 install apps and keeping the instance from reaching the remote app
                 repository - are assessed under SRG-APP-000810-AU-000250.

external:        Signing of app and module packages and verification of that signature
                 before installation, carried by the package producer and by the
                 organization's app review and approval procedure.
external:        Separation of development and test work from the production instance,
                 carried by the deployment design rather than by any setting on the
                 instance.
external:        Ownership and modes on the app directories, which keep an unreviewed
                 module from being placed there, carried by the operating system.

manual_reason:   No .conf setting in the 10.4.2 specification set governs the review, test,
                 or signature state of an app or expansion module, and the check inventory
                 attaches no conf/stanza/key to this requirement. There is nothing in the
                 application's configuration for a condition to read.

citation:        Web Server SRG SRG-APP-000131-WSR-000073 check and fix text; absence of
                 any governing setting across the 10.4.2 specification set (app.conf.spec,
                 authorize.conf.spec, limits.conf.spec)
finding:         Not a finding against the application: Splunk exposes no setting bearing
                 on module review, testing, or signing. Record the organization's app
                 review and package signing procedure as the responsible control, and note
                 that the application cannot enforce it.
